    <briefdescription>
<para>Receives process, exception, breakpoint, and module-load events from dbgeng. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Registered with IDebugClient5::SetEventCallbacks. Each handled callback fires an event on <ref refid="classdebug_1_1_session_1a81f6eec8b52b3becaada99d133d8840f" kindref="member">Session::events</ref> and returns a status that tells dbgeng whether to keep the target stopped. Callbacks run on the engine context, inside WaitForEvent.</para>
<para><ref refid="namespacedebug_1afb8f56694e0d51f128a832c3a0c91042" kindref="member">Events</ref> that each callback fires:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Breakpoint → breakpoint, with the engine breakpoint id. Returns DEBUG_STATUS_BREAK.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Exception → EXCEPTION_BREAKPOINT fires initialBreak while launching, pause while isPausePending, and exception otherwise. Other codes fire exception on a second-chance notification only.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>LoadModule → moduleLoad, with the image name, unless a step is pending.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>ExitProcess → exited, with the exit code.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>CreateProcess → targetProcessId, with the process id.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>GetInterestMask selects the breakpoint, exception, create-process, exit-process, and load-module events. dbgeng never invokes the other methods.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>Owned by <ref refid="classdebug_1_1_session" kindref="compound">Session</ref> as a member. setDebugInterfaces registers it, and shutdown unregisters it. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
